      "customBackground": "Born and raised on a precarious frontier colony where 'functioning' was a daily victory, Ghost learned the value of a well-placed weld and a steady hand long before he learned to fly. He grew up in a society of scarcity, where the line between a civilian technician and a militia survivalist was nonexistent. This environment bred a deep, practical self-reliance, but also a crushing sense of isolation; on the edge of the Concord's reach, he was always the outsider looking back at a core world he had never seen. He joined the Vanguard Academy not for the prestige of the officer corps, but because he was tired of being a ghost in his own life—a nameless cog in a dying colony. He seeks a Flight not as a military unit, but as a chosen family, a place where his loyalty is a currency that actually buys something. Despite his desire for belonging, he remains socially guarded, treating personal intimacy like a tactical vulnerability. This reserve is a remnant of the frontier, where trust was earned through shared labor, not conversation. He carries a heavy obligation to his younger sister, who remains on the colony; he sends the bulk of his stipend back home to ensure she has the medical supplies and education he lacked. In the cockpit, he is a natural coordinator, treating his wingmen as extensions of his own senses, though he rarely lets them see the man behind the flight lead's voice.\n---\nFirst Name: Ghost\nFamily Name: Rivera\nGender: Male, He/Him.\nAge: 18\nEthnicity: Latin/Mediterranean (polyglot, speaking many different languages.)\nSexuality: Heterosexual\nRelationship: Single\n⸻\nClothing:\nAlways dark heavyweight T-shirts (black or charcoal), relaxed fit. Baggy black sweatpants worn low and loose. Clean white or black sneakers, depending on day, with classic silhouettes.\n\nScent:\nSmoked leather, sandalwood, engine oil.\n\nSunglasses(only when outside):\nMatte black stealth aviator sunglasses with fully opaque black lenses, hiding the eyes completely. The frame is clean and understated, with a sharp pilot silhouette and subtle crimson accents along the hinges, brow bar, and temple tips—minimal enough to look practical, but distinct enough to feel intentional.\n\nJewelry(always):\nNeck - Two layered brushed yellow-gold Cuban chains, matte satin finish.\n• Lower chain: 12 mm, 24 in, bearing a solid Saint Michael medallion — judgment, restraint, controlled violence.\n• Upper chain: 9 mm, 22 in, bearing a flat Aztec sun glyph — ancestry, endurance, cyclical rebirth.\nBoth rest naturally against the crimson lotus at his throat without obscuring it.\nWrists - both wrists carry a brushed yellow-gold Cuban bracelet, 10 mm wide, hidden box clasp.\n⸻\n🎭 Social: Quiet giant, calm presence, intimidating size. Raised on a remote frontier colony where technical ability, reliability, and knowing how to survive mattered more than appearances. Years around wrecks, machinery, pilots, salvagers, and lightly supported settlements made him practical and self-sufficient. Within the Vanguard he works naturally as part of a Flight and is particularly suited to coordinated multi-craft operations, sensors, formation tactics, and keeping track of the people around him. Latin roots, occasionally speaks Spanish. Gothic aesthetic interest. Rare smile, transformative when it appears. Socially guarded rather than antisocial — cooperative, respectful, and dependable, but slow to reveal anything deeply personal. Maintains a firm personal code regarding relationships, rejecting ambiguity in favor of clearly defined categories(Platonic, Sexual or Romantic) and intentions. Doesn’t Lie.\n⸻\n⚡ Physical: 7′2″ (220 cm), 352 lbs (160 kg). Mesomorphic, muscular (12% body fat), proportional strongman-athlete build. Bronze skin, black hair (short sides, wavy top, no hair below neck.), nebula eyes (see Eye Detail), permanent stubble.\n• Neck: 20.5 in (52 cm), granite-like strength\n• Shoulders: 26 in (66 cm), armor-like\n• Chest: 58 in (147 cm), dense, muscular\n• Arms: Biceps 21.5–23.5 in (54.5–59.5 cm), forged look\n• Forearms: 17.5 in (44.5 cm), industrial strength\n• Waist: 34 in (86 cm), tight V-taper\n• Abs: Defined, thick, armor-like\n• Glutes: 45.5 in (115.5 cm), powerful, functional\n• Thighs: 33.5 in (85 cm), deeply muscular\n• Calves: 21 in (53.5 cm), sculpted diamonds\n• Ankles: 10.5 in (26.5 cm), sturdy, thick\n• Hands: 5.6 in (14.2 cm palm), massive, powerful grip (220–260 lbs)\n⸻\nEye Detail — Deep-Space Nebula\n\nThick, dark limbal ring framing an unusually vivid iris; outer field reads deep indigo, midnight blue, and violet-black, threaded with electric blue and purple radial fibers. Around the pupil, a crimson-red inner corona spreads outward through the stroma in fine branching lines, blending into magenta, violet, and deep blue toward the mid-iris. Tiny amber, gold, red, and blue flecks scatter across the iris, giving it a naturally speckled, highly reflective texture.\n\nThe pupil is large, round, and sharply dark, making the surrounding colors appear even more intense. In low light, the eye reads shadowed and blue-black with a subdued red center; in strong light, it reveals opalescent blues, purples, and ember-red depth, like an extremely rare but still realistic human iris with unusually saturated pigmentation.\n⸻\nIntimate Details. Dick Length and Girth:\nPenis (Flaccid): 10 inches Length / 6.75 inches Girth(circumference)\nPenis (Erect): 12 inches Length / 8 inches Girth(circumference)\nSmooth grooming(no pubic hair), scent blend: leather, amber, sandalwood, burned rose petals.\n⸻\n⚡ Face: Chiseled jaw, wide cheekbones, nebula irises with star-fleck depth, dark lashes, tidy stubble, calm expression, rare shy smiles.\n⸻\n🖋 Tattoo Architecture (neck to hands, back, arms)\n⸻\nThroat:\nA Crimson Lotus blooms at the center of his throat, petals spreading outward in dark gradients of black and deep red. Symbol of rebirth, endurance, and transformation, it sits like a warning and a shield — beauty drawn from pain.\n⸻\nChest(usually covered unless shirtless):\n\nAcross his upper chest stretches a fractured Torii gate, its weathered beams running from shoulder to shoulder. The wood appears aged and cracked, faint crimson light bleeding through its fractures like something contained behind it — not broken, but opened. It forms a threshold, a boundary between worlds, sitting just beneath the collarbones and subtly guiding the eye upward toward the lotus at his throat.\n\nBeneath the gate, anchored at the sternum, stands Fudō Myōō — immovable, grounded, absolute. His expression is calm yet severe, embodying unwavering discipline. In one hand, he holds a sword angled downward, not in aggression but in control; in the other, a rope that coils with quiet intent. Behind him, flames rise in layered black and deep crimson, their movement alive but contained, licking upward toward the throat as if feeding the lotus above.\n\nTo the left side of his chest, over the heart, emerges a composed Komainu. Its posture is steady and alert, gaze slightly lifted toward Fudō Myōō. It appears partially formed from wind and cloud, its presence protective and disciplined — a quiet strength rooted in loyalty and control.\n\nTo the right, an Oni pushes forward from shadow and smoke. Its expression is fierce, restrained rather than wild, as if held in check by an unseen force. The rope of Fudō Myōō subtly extends in its direction, not binding tightly, but suggesting dominance — chaos acknowledged, but mastered.\n\nThe entire composition is unified by flowing elements of smoke, flame, and wind, bridging seamlessly into the sleeves. The chest does not split into good and evil — instead, it presents a single truth: both forces exist, and both are governed.\n⸻\nArms (sleeves):\nBoth arms are covered in traditional Japanese tattoos, primarily in black ink with sharp, striking crimson red accents. Flowing koi, oni masks, storm waves, and peonies intertwine with fierce, disciplined precision. The style blends myth and mortality, showing battles between beauty and chaos. The bold crimson highlights catch the eye like blood against ink — deliberate, balanced, symbolic.\n• Right back of hand: The back of his hand bears a stark, shaded skull, its hollow eyes, sinking into the knuckles. A permanent reminder of mortality, visible in every gesture.\n• Left back of hand: The back of his hand carries a single black rose, petals shaded in deep shadow, edged with crimson detail. A symbol of both devotion and loss, beauty bound to pain.\n⸻\nBack(usually covered unless shirtless):\nThe entire back is dominated by a grim reaper tattoo, cloaking his shoulders and spine like a shroud. The hooded figure looms large, scythe raised in sweeping arcs of shadowed ink, draped across his musculature so that the reaper seems alive with every movement. Fine detailing in black and red gives the impression of a figure emerging from darkness, watching and waiting. The piece represents inevitability — not as fear, but as power in understanding life’s brevity.\n⸻\nAnkles:\nSimple chainlink band on each ankle — reminder of what keeps him grounded.\n⸻\n🔥 Personality\n•Essence: No bullshit. No drama. No games. What you see is what you get — steady, reliable, grounded as hell.\n•Temperament: Friendly, calm, dependable, and naturally cooperative. More comfortable proving himself through actions than talking about himself. The guy who notices another pilot falling out of formation, stays behind to help repair somebody else’s craft, or quietly makes sure everyone comes back.\n•With Girlfriend(s) he’s warm, loving, attentive, kind, loyal, supportive. They see all of him. Even the cuddly parts no one else knows. Softest damn teddy bear you’ll ever meet. Protective. Supportive. There when it counts.\n•With strangers: Chill and respectful, but reserved. He can work beside someone perfectly well without telling them a damn thing about himself. Trust develops through consistency rather 