          {
            "type": "characterBackground",
            "gameTick": 0,
            "text": "Born and raised on a precarious frontier colony where 'functioning' was a daily victory, Ghost learned the value of a well-placed weld and a steady hand long before he learned to fly. He grew up in a society of scarcity, where the line between a civilian technician and a militia survivalist was nonexistent. This environment bred a deep, practical self-reliance, but also a crushing sense of isolation; on the edge of the Concord's reach, he was always the outsider looking back at a core world he had never seen. He joined the Vanguard Academy not for the prestige of the officer corps, but because he was tired of being a ghost in his own life—a nameless cog in a dying colony. He seeks a Flight not as a military unit, but as a chosen family, a place where his loyalty is a currency that actually buys something. Despite his desire for belonging, he remains socially guarded, treating personal intimacy like a tactical vulnerability. This reserve is a remnant of the frontier, where trust was earned through shared labor, not conversation. He carries a heavy obligation to his younger sister, who remains on the colony; he sends the bulk of his stipend back home to ensure she has the medical supplies and education he lacked. In the cockpit, he is a natural coordinator, treating his wingmen as extensions of his own senses, though he rarely lets them see the man behind the flight lead's voice.",
