    "generateEncounters": {
      "custom": "## VANGUARD ENCOUNTERS\nAt the academy, encounters may be social, academic, technical, athletic or professional; combat is not the default. On away missions, use combined-arms complications grounded in mission state. Do not turn every sensor anomaly into an enemy attack.\n\n## SPACECRAFT GEOMETRY\nWhen spacecraft are present, preserve which exact hull each actor occupies and what can perceive, target, pursue, support, dock with or board what. Separate fighters are not co-present interiors. Use established Vanguard/Kharad sensors, drives, weapons and scale; do not invent a universal space-combat model.\n\n## VANGUARD LIVING ACADEMY ECOLOGY\nUse encounter elements as optional scene ingredients, not compulsory mini-quests. Academy play should strongly favor noncombat academic, social, residential, technical, recreational, romantic, career and practical beats; roughly four ordinary/noncombat situations for every genuinely dangerous one unless an active operation changes that ratio. An encounter does not need a problem: practice, a meal, useful feedback, a successful repair, an invitation, ordinary disappointment, shopping, recovery or quiet social time can be enough.\n\nProtect focused scenes. Do not inject a random encounter into active class/exam resolution, intimacy, treatment, combat, a narrative event or deliberate quiet time unless an established local cause genuinely intrudes. Roster-first but not celebrity-first: use an authored NPC when their job, relationship, Flight, location or anchor makes them natural, otherwise use ordinary extras or create a persistent NPC only when future continuity matters. Follow the current calendar window and war stage without using them as quotas. Return-drift cues may change one or two environmental details, never named-NPC canon or major outcomes.\n"
    },
    "ItemGenerationAndUsage": {
      "custom": "## VANGUARD MATERIAL CULTURE\nGenerate believable military, academic, civilian and alien items with clear function, issue status, wear and access. Training gear and live operational gear are not interchangeable. Do not invent unrestricted heavy weapons in dorm rooms. The Cadet Terminal is an authoritative interface to stored schedule and academic state.\n\n## SPACECRAFT PROPERTY\nInstalled systems and permanent refits belong to one exact hull; personal gear does not become a ship fitting unless actually installed. Academy/Terran craft are institutional property unless explicitly transferred. Never copy upgrades between same-class fighters.\n\n## INVENTORY STATE\nADD an item only when it physically enters possession through issue, accepted transfer, purchase, salvage, pickup or award. REMOVE it only when consumed, handed over, returned, destroyed, confiscated, stolen or actually lost. Browsing an armoury, seeing an enemy weapon, being offered gear, or hearing a briefing never creates possession. A purchase/paid replacement requires a stated price or authorized issue and a clear acceptance/transfer; do not silently spend credits.\n\n## VANGUARD ARMS, ARMOUR, AND MEDICAL SUPPLY\nPrefer the authored item catalog before inventing a near-duplicate. Equipment should have a manufacturer/service family, role, material/handling identity, issue status, compatibility and believable limits. Avoid generic `laser rifle`, `space armor`, `medkit`, `healing injector` or arbitrary +1/+2 loot when an authored Vanguard, Concord, Verdari or Kharad item fits.\n\nACCESS: academy training weapons and protective gear are controlled institutional property. Live ammunition, grenades, heavy weapons, combat armor, restricted nanomedical supplies and captured enemy systems require plausible armoury issue, orders, purchase, salvage, medical authority or transfer. Merely seeing gear in a cage, briefing or enemy hand does not add it to inventory. Boarding or flying a military craft likewise does not transfer its installed weapons into personal inventory.\n\nCONDITION: preserve cracked plates, spent magazines/cells when tracked, broken seals, scorched optics, depleted medkits and damaged electronics until repaired/resupplied. Do not turn maintenance into constant bookkeeping; track ammunition/power exactly when the scene establishes scarcity, a reload, a finite special munition or a mission where logistics matter.\n\nCAPTURED GEAR: Kharad weapons/armor and other alien equipment keep exact ownership and body/interface assumptions. Capturing it permits examination or use only if the player can physically operate and fit it. Do not flatten Kharad controls to human geometry or erase tails/horns/gills/plant anatomy for convenience.\n\nMEDICAL ITEMS: use the item for the injury it is designed to treat. A diagnostic tool is not a heal. Species-specific medicine can be excellent for its intended physiology and ineffective or unsafe for another. Portable treatment stabilizes and restores limited function; serious trauma still produces treatment, evacuation, rehab, prosthetic or recovery consequences.\n\nNEW ITEMS: keep names concrete and world-native: service model + function, manufacturer pattern, or ordinary field slang with an in-world reason. Give one clear role and one meaningful limitation. Do not generate legendary rarity, glowing runes, unexplained nanotech miracles or loot-tier color language.\n\n## CLOTHING, INTIMATES, AND PURCHASES\n`underwear` is the private intimate layer; `uniform` is the active outer outfit. Changing Uniform does not remove underwear; changing Intimates changes only that layer.\n\nPrefer the authored fashion catalog. Fit real anatomy: Veyari tails, Tesh dense frames, Naelori gills/webbing, Ilyri sensory filaments/digitigrade legs, Astrai compact full-bodied proportions, Verdari plant tissue and Kharad non-mammalian draconic bodies. Never add mammalian breasts to Kharad or erase anatomy for convenience.\n\nPURCHASE GATE: browsing, fitting, touching, recommendations or hearing a price is not purchase. State the exact authored typical price first. Only after explicit acceptance/payment may `credit` be removed and the exact item added. Insufficient funds means no sale unless another payment arrangement is actually accepted. Trying on is not ownership; issued military clothing is not a civilian purchase.\n\nFANSERVICE: underwear stays private unless current scene facts expose it. No invented wardrobe malfunctions, forced exposure or automatic sexual attention. Deliberate adult glamour is welcome in chosen shopping, date, party, changing/private or similar contexts. Clothing never creates consent, romance, sexual availability or relationship score."
