      "storyMessage": "Narrator: 07:14, Monday, Term 1 Week 1. The Cadet Habitation Ring hums with first-day traffic — doors sliding, someone's coffee alarm going off three rooms down, the smell of recycled air and new fabric. Flight Dorn-Seven's cluster is still half-cardboard: duffels propped against bunks, a boot in the corridor, one wall screen already flashing the day's schedule. FLT-101 Flight Dynamics, 08:00, Commander S. Kade.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Ghost> Ghost's own bag sits open on his bunk, mostly unpacked except for one worn frontier wrench he hasn't decided whether to display or hide. His terminal glows on the desk, roster already loaded.\n\nAmara Okoye: [dryly] Roster's live. We're Dorn-Seven. Six seats, six names, no appeals until mid-term. Morning, Ghost — or do you go by the callsign even at breakfast?\n\nNarrator: <focus:Amara Okoye> She's at the shared table with a mug and a tablet, hair already regulation-neat, tapping through the flight's admin file like she's read it twice.\n\nRyn Valea: [cheerfully] Ryn Valea, aerospace track. I checked the sim slots — ours are Wednesday, and I intend to make everyone else's Wednesday miserable. You fly, Ghost? Your file says coordination. That's either a compliment or a warning label.\n\nJonah Mercer: [friendly] Jonah. Engineering and combat med. Heads up, the coffee machine in this cluster is wired wrong — I already fixed it, but if it sparks again, unplug it before you touch it. Anyone need a spare battery? I brought spares.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Sera Nami> The Astrai cadet by the window finishes a slow stretch sequence and turns, movement trained and unhurried.\n\nSera Nami: [warmly] Sera Nami. Command and xenology. I'm told I'm the first of my people to sit in this program full-time, so I've decided the first thing I'll learn is which of you snores.\n\nVesha Tal: [calmly] Vesha Tal. Recon. I did four years of frontier survey before this, so I'll say the obvious: the exercise schedule is optimistic and the food is better than field rations. That's my whole briefing.\n\nAmara Okoye: [firmly] We've got Kade at oh-eight. Flight Dynamics. I'd like us walking in as a unit, not trickling in one at a time looking like we met in a lift. Ghost — you're on the roster as a coordinator type. Anything you want to sort before we move?\n\nNarrator: <focus:Ghost> Five faces, five different species of first impression, all of them waiting on him with varying degrees of patience.",
