      "storyMessage": "⏰ 08:20 • T1 W1 Mon • Morning • 📍 Vanguard Joint Expeditionary Academy • 🎓 FLT-101 Flight Dynamics • 🟢 Routine\n\nNarrator: <focus:Ghost> Ghost's hand settles on Ryn's head, fingers kneading slow circles between her ears while his free hand comes up.\n\nGhost: [dry] Question. You said us missing a session isn't a scheduling issue but a leadership issue. So if one of us misses a session, that's your fault then — considering you hold the leadership position?\n\nNarrator: <focus:Commander Seraphine Kade> Kade turns from the display wall, unhurried, and lets the pause stretch long enough to be an answer in itself.\n\nCommander Kade: [calmly] No. Leadership at this level means you make it possible for your people to be prepared — rosters, briefings, accountability. It does not mean I crawl into your bunk and drag you out of it. If a cadet misses a session, I ask the Flight lead one question: did you know? If yes, the failure is shared. If no, the failure is yours for not knowing.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Ryn Valea> Ryn melts into the scalp massage with a soft, breathy laugh, purring low enough that only Ghost can feel it through his palm.\n\nRyn Valea: [whispering, teasing] Careful with the logic, honey. If I'm the leader, that just means I get to decide exactly how we're punished for missing class — and I can think of a few things much more interesting than a lecture.\n\nAmara Okoye: [sharply, low] Enough. Both of you. If I hear one more word about \"punishment\" or \"kittens\" while Kade is looking this way, I'm reporting you for conduct unbecoming before the first bell even rings.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Commander Seraphine Kade> Kade's grey-green eyes sweep the back row and stop there, holding.\n\nCommander Kade: [dryly] Since the back row seems to have discovered a fascinating topic that outweighs formation geometry, perhaps one of you would like to come up here and explain the primary weakness of a tight line-abreast formation under high-G maneuvers?\n\nNarrator: <focus:Ryn Valea> Ryn's ears flatten against Ghost's retreating hand, and she sits up straight with the speed of a cadet who just realized the spotlight found her row.\n\nRyn Valea: [brightly, unbothered] That would be me, Commander.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Ghost> Ghost leans back, arms crossing, one brow rising in open amusement as Ryn slides out of her seat and heads for the front of the hall.",
