      "storyMessage": "⏰ 08:30 • T1 W1 Mon • Morning • 📍 Vanguard Joint Expeditionary Academy • 🎓 FLT-101 Flight Dynamics • 🟢 Routine\n\nNarrator: <focus:Ghost> Ghost waits until Ryn is halfway down the steps, attention locked on the display wall, then cups a hand near his mouth and lets out a low, rolling \"pspsps\" — pitched just under the room's ambient hum, aimed at her ears alone.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Ryn Valea> Her tail snaps upright mid-stride, ears swiveling back toward the back row before she can stop them. She shoots Ghost a look that promises murder wrapped in glitter, then plants herself before the display wall with her chin high.\n\nRyn Valea: [brightly, refusing to blush] Yes, well. Tight line-abreast under high-G — the outer wingmen run out of turn radius first. Everyone's pulling the same angle, but the ships on the outside of the arc have to cover more distance at the same speed, so their spacing collapses inward. You get midair compression, wingtip overlaps, and one bad correction away from two fighters eating each other.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Commander Seraphine Kade> Kade steps aside without a word, giving Ryn the floor, her expression giving away nothing as she studies the answer.\n\nCommander Kade: [after a measured pause] Correct. Compression, not collision — compression is what kills you, because it happens before anyone sees it. [dryly] Which is why line-abreast tightens only under controlled closure, never under sustained high-G. Sit down, Cadet Valea. And whatever your Flightmate said to make your tail do that — I saw it. Save it for the sim.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Ryn Valea> Ryn struts back up the tiers with an unrepentant grin, tail swaying in slow, deliberate arcs, and drops into her seat beside Ghost.\n\nRyn Valea: [whispering, teasing] You're a menace, honey. Pspsps. At me. In Kade's class. [ears flicking, mock outrage] You owe me a scalp massage for that, minimum.\n\nAmara Okoye: [muttering, low, eyes forward] Six days in and we're already the row Kade remembers. Wonderful.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Commander Seraphine Kade> Kade taps the display wall again; the four-fighter mesh dissolves into a rotating echelon wedge, vectors trailing in crimson.\n\nCommander Kade: [firmly] Echelon wedge. Draw it, label the lead's protection sectors, and tell me why the trailing wingman on the short side has the worst job in the formation. You have four minutes. Back row — I'm watching you twice as hard now.",
