      "storyMessage": "Narrator: <focus:Ghost> Ghost shrugs and does what Kade said — pulls up a sketch surface on the terminal and starts drawing the echelon wedge, vectors and protection sectors laid out with the neat economy of someone who's briefed formations for real.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Amara Okoye> One row over, Amara's drawing tool opens with clinical precision, lines snapping to exact angles as she works.\n\nAmara Okoye: [murmuring, barely audible] Eyes on the task. All of us. Kade's already picked her example row — let's not give her a second reason.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Ryn Valea> Ryn leans over, shoulder pressing warm against Ghost's arm as she sketches on her own screen, tail curling around the base of his seat.\n\nRyn Valea: [whispering, playful] You're definitely on massage duty tonight, honey. I can feel the tension in my ears already.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Commander Seraphine Kade> Kade paces slowly along the front, saying nothing, her gaze flicking to the back row at intervals while the countdown timer on the display wall ticks down — three minutes, two.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Ryn Valea> Ryn's screen fills with a wedge that looks beautiful and is subtly wrong — her short-side trailing wingman sits inside the lead's protection sector instead of outside it.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Ghost> Ghost catches it out of the corner of his eye, but his own wedge is drawn to spec and he keeps his eyes forward, letting her figure it out.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Commander Seraphine Kade> The timer hits zero and Kade stops pacing, turning to face the hall.\n\nCommander Kade: [firmly] Time. Terminals up, diagrams facing me. I'll walk the rows — and I'll start at the back.",
