      "storyMessage": "Narrator: <focus:Ghost> Ghost gives Sera and Vesha one last playful wink, then turns to his console and goes still. The smirk fades. His hands settle on stick and throttle, and everything else in the hall drops away — nothing but geometry, timing, and the wireframe waiting on his board.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Commander Seraphine Kade> Kade's voice rolls over the net, flat and even.\n\nCommander Kade: [calmly] Ten seconds. Ships one through three, your break points are live. Four through six, net discipline. Watch your clocks.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Ryn Valea> Ryn's teasing evaporates the instant the countdown starts. Her ears pin flat, claws settling with surgical care on the controls, and she locks her eyes on her assigned break bearing — nothing in her posture left but intent.\n\nRyn Valea: [flat, focused] Ship two, ready. Holding for my mark.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Amara Okoye> Amara squares her shoulders over her terminal, spine rigid, running her stagger timing in a silent rhythm. Her own trace sits perfectly in echelon, a model line for the row to follow.\n\nAmara Okoye: [crisp] Ship one, ready. Lead break on your mark, Commander.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Commander Seraphine Kade> Kade watches the wall, then keys the net.\n\nCommander Kade: [sharply] Mark. Lead — break.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Amara Okoye> Amara's wireframe snaps into the break at exactly her mark, the arc carving wide and clean as she pulls combat spread through the recovery.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Commander Seraphine Kade> Four seconds later, Kade's voice again.\n\nCommander Kade: [sharply] Ship two — break.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Ryn Valea> Ryn throws her break with the precision of a blade leaving a sheath — her arc mirrors Amara's timing to the tenth of a second, spacing held through the pullout without a single degree of drift.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Commander Seraphine Kade> Six seconds after the lead, the third call.\n\nCommander Kade: [sharply] Ship three — break.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Ghost> Ghost's break comes on his clock exactly — no flourish, no wasted input. His wireframe slices into the staggered arc, threading the gap between Amara's and Ryn's recovery lines, and settles into combat spread as if the maneuver had been rehearsed a hundred times.",
